"><name><surname>Coiera</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Dowton</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Editorial: Re-inventing Ourselves &#x02013; How on-line 'just-in-time' CME may help bring about a genuinely evidence-based clinical practice</article-title><source>Medical Journal of Australia</source><year>2000</year><volume>173</volume><fpage>343</fpage><lpage>344</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11062787</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Coiera</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><source>Information economics and the Internet Journal of the American Medical Informatics Association</source><year>2000</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>215</fpage><lpage>221</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Balasubramanian</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Wiener</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Alshameeri</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Tiruvoipati</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Elbourne</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Reed</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Standards of reporting of randomized controlled trials in general surgery: can we do better?</article-title><source>Annals of Surgery</source><year>2006</year><volume>244</volume><fpage>663</fpage><lpage>667</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17060756</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.sla.0000217640.11224.05</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boots</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Dalen</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuin</surname><giv